        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm strongly opposed to the others saying arm length should be default. Scale by height is much easier to understand, much more consistent between avatars and makes User Real Height as a setting make sense. \nBased on my experience I believe it should be default.\nWhen I starting out easily the most confusing part was that floor position never matched up, and varied per avatar. Even as a tech savvy creator it took a lot of mental gymnastics to realize world scale is dependent on arm length. I feel like aligning the virtual floor with the real floor is VR application design 101.\nAs a both long time 3pt tracking user, and a relatively new 6pt tracking user I felt a sigh of relief when I realized every single avatar I use is now properly fitted with scale by height, and the User Real Height setting makes sense and needs to be at my actual real height, not some arbitrary number that's a compromise between arm length and hips/feet/floor position. Hands detaching due to arms being too short is easy to understand and it's really not as big of a deal as people make it out to be, feels sort of like how it would make sense to build a costume in real life.\nAlso I would argue that height does have tracking data: the HMD. Scale is relative in VR so the only measure in addition to horizontal translation you have is distance off the floor, so it's important that the floor position matches or you feel like you're floating.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
