      "postID": "621eec242e157875baa5ad47",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Its all about the first impressions.\nI don't think measure by height should be the default for non-fullbody.\nIn 3 point tracking, the arms matching is vital for first timers. That's where the magic is. The wingspan matching even for non-proportioned avatars is vital for the vast majority of users, who are not FBT and really don't care about the floor height.\nThere are many avatars with short or crazy long arms and having these arms feel right in 3PT is way more important than you think.\nFBT is a power user feature. We know how to change it to measure by height.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
