      "value": "@{5f50687837bf962e69ae2921|full_name}: I was about to leave a comment in favor of keeping the default as arm-scale, but after reading your comment I’m not sure. \nLike you, when I started VRChat for the first time, I immediately noticed the incongruous floor heights (especially perceivable with permanent floor bounds enabled in chaperone) and assumed it was a bug, since none of my other VR games behaved this way. While searching for a fix, I learned about arm-scaling. \nThe reason behind the mismatched floors was not immediately intuitive for me, and looking back, I probably would have been less confused with height-scaling and short in-game arms.\nHeight-scaling isn’t perfect though. For avatars with inhuman legs, the world looking so small or big is unsettling. With arm-scaling, the floor difference for these avatars is so large that I think it  is not as unintuitive as more reasonably proportioned avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
