        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have to say that one upside from scaling by height is that changing your height in the settings does exactly what it says to do, it changes your height. Arm-Span in comparison changes your arm-span which can be a bit confusing if the setting you are changing is called \"User Real Height\". At lot of people (me included) always changed their height with the old IK so that the length of their feet is fitting and not that the length of their arms are fitting. \nTo get around that confusion you could consider adding a tool tip when looking at the IK settings for the first time which tells people that scaling by height means their avatar height will always fit and that scaling by arm-span will always make the length of their arms fit.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
